WEBVTT

00:02.326 --> 00:03.667
Hey guys, it's Dee again.

00:03.987 --> 00:06.809
Last time I barely survived the Jurassic Zoo.

00:07.109 --> 00:12.933
This time I snuck back in and saw unrealistic dinosaurs no one has ever seen before.

00:13.253 --> 00:16.955
But one incident happened that shut the whole park down forever.

00:17.316 --> 00:19.317
Stick till the end, you won't believe it.

00:19.857 --> 00:21.058
Hey guys, it's Dee again.

00:21.758 --> 00:24.340
Last time I barely survived the Jurassic Zoo.

00:25.901 --> 00:26.762
Can I get discount?

00:27.722 --> 00:29.223
No, it's same for everyone.

00:30.264 --> 00:31.505
Sad, but okay.

00:32.538 --> 00:33.679
There's quite a crowd today.

00:34.820 --> 00:36.821
Looks like they're here to see something special.

00:38.482 --> 00:39.102
Are they mad?

00:39.282 --> 00:40.843
They put all the dangerous ones together?

00:41.344 --> 00:41.984
What's in that?

00:42.905 --> 00:48.588
Carnotaurus used its horns to fight other carnotaurus for territory and maintenance.

00:48.829 --> 00:53.852
Honestly, other large carnivores were the biggest threat to baby carnotaurus.

00:55.705 --> 00:58.226
Who was the actual rival of Carnotaurus?

00:58.726 --> 01:00.587
I'll let the audience answer that one.

01:00.607 --> 01:07.689
Fun fact, Carnotaurus had some of the smallest arms compared to its body size of any large theropod dinosaur.

01:07.869 --> 01:08.310
See that?

01:08.970 --> 01:10.810
She's probably a better mother than yours.

01:13.912 --> 01:17.773
Carnotaurus usually lived alone and could reach about 25 years of age.

01:20.574 --> 01:21.734
What an interesting question.

01:22.035 --> 01:22.975
Audience should answer this.

01:30.348 --> 01:31.648
Please keep safe distance.

01:32.188 --> 01:35.209
Spinosaurus can react quickly to movement near the enclosure.

01:36.469 --> 01:42.010
Some scientists think young spinosaurus may have spent more time on land than adults, but this is still debated.

01:42.550 --> 01:46.191
Its possible rival was carcordontosaurus, but what do you think?

01:48.371 --> 01:54.412
Spinosaurus mainly ate fish, occasionally crocodiles and small dinosaurs, and likely consumed around 70 to 150 kilograms of food per day.

01:59.383 --> 02:03.285
Young spinosaurus likely stayed under their mother's protection for several years.

02:07.968 --> 02:10.150
Who knows, maybe they left a mosasaurus in there.

02:12.851 --> 02:16.814
Movies made therosinosaurus look like a pure predator, but it was probably mostly herbivorous.

02:17.514 --> 02:22.217
Honestly, some scientists think baby therosinosaurus were meaner than the adults.

02:24.909 --> 02:26.569
Those claws look terrifying.

02:27.270 --> 02:28.750
And it's still mostly eight plants.

02:29.110 --> 02:32.791
Tarbasaurus was probably one of its biggest rivals.

02:36.992 --> 02:37.913
That's huge.

02:38.413 --> 02:39.733
I still huge.

02:39.793 --> 02:41.374
No, it was a dinosaur picture.

02:41.394 --> 02:43.034
Look at the wingspan.

02:44.915 --> 02:48.816
Did you know baby Quetzalcatlus can start flying just minutes after hatching?

02:49.196 --> 02:49.756
No way.

02:56.981 --> 03:02.884
One of Quetzalcoatlis' biggest rivals was Hatsagopterics, another giant tyrosaur that lived during the late Cretaceous period.

03:03.164 --> 03:07.967
Scientists estimate Quetzalcoatlis may have lived around 20 to 30 years on average.

03:15.180 --> 03:21.086
Velociraptors likely hatched covered in feathers, making them look more like young birds than the scaly dinosaurs.

03:21.286 --> 03:24.669
A likely rival of Velociraptor was protoceratops.

03:25.430 --> 03:31.115
Fossils have even been discovered showing a Velociraptor and protoceratops locked together during a fight.

03:31.216 --> 03:33.238
Can I give them some chicken nuggets?

03:34.379 --> 03:35.920
I don't think the zoo allows that.

03:37.201 --> 03:38.543
They probably want the whole bucket.

03:48.031 --> 03:50.473
Finally, an enclosure of peaceful dinos.

03:53.316 --> 03:59.201
Interesting fact, an Argentinosaurus may have needed roughly 100 to 150 kilograms of vegetation every day to support its enormous size.

04:01.142 --> 04:03.204
Brachiosaurus had no long-term relationships.

04:03.544 --> 04:05.186
Mating was brief and seasonal only.

04:08.669 --> 04:12.132
Ankylosaurus probably spent a lot of time resting.

04:14.644 --> 04:16.666
Diplodocus was the friend of Stegosaurus.

04:17.046 --> 04:19.788
They lived together peacefully, eating plant side by side.

04:22.431 --> 04:23.371
Can I ride this one?

04:26.794 --> 04:32.419
Most people don't know sauripods probably swallowed rocks called gastrolis to help grind food inside their stomachs.

04:40.526 --> 04:42.588
Maybe there's Mosasaurus feeding time.

04:46.659 --> 04:47.199
This way, ma'am.

04:50.940 --> 04:56.042
Mosasaurus likely spent much of its time cruising slowly through ancient oceans.

05:02.503 --> 05:05.544
I wonder what killed the Mosasaurus more than anything else.

05:07.705 --> 05:12.046
Plesiosaurus used all four flippers to swim, almost like underwater flying.

05:18.485 --> 05:24.029
Mosasaurus had a second set of teeth on the roof of its mouth that helped pull prey deeper into its throat.

05:24.449 --> 05:27.171
Do you think these two could actually live together?

05:33.275 --> 05:35.297
That thing is even bigger than I expected.

05:45.300 --> 05:46.001
Nice packaging.

05:49.844 --> 05:51.265
Can we pet any dinosaurs?

05:55.988 --> 05:58.670
Was T-Rex really the king of dinosaurs?

06:01.012 --> 06:05.276
Some scientists think triceratops may have been one of T-Rex's toughest rivals.

06:05.516 --> 06:09.559
A T-Rex tooth could reach over 30 centimeters long, including the root.

06:24.490 --> 06:28.832
Tyrannosaurus rex had one of the strongest bite forces of any known land animal.

06:35.694 --> 06:36.915
I'm afraid to go in there.

06:39.836 --> 06:43.017
Indomnis rex are more intelligent than many humans.

06:46.582 --> 06:51.744
If Indominus Rex had camouflage abilities, sudden fast attacks from cover would effective than chasing prey over long distance.

06:51.764 --> 06:52.605
Here's a debated theory.

06:52.725 --> 06:57.727
Camouflage may have been one of the most powerful advantages an Indominus Rex could have had, possibly even more important than its size.

07:03.829 --> 07:04.209
Do you know?

07:04.709 --> 07:10.952
Before Indominus Rex, the Jurassic World team originally planned the main hybrid as Diabolus Rex, or D-Rex in early scripts.

07:11.272 --> 07:12.973
They later changed it to Indominus Rex.

07:14.808 --> 07:18.549
I don't know why I'm here, whether to enjoy this or suffer through it.

07:20.810 --> 07:22.851
People think he's a monster, but is he?

07:46.013 --> 07:46.554
Attention!

07:47.014 --> 07:48.916
Evacuate immediately!

07:48.996 --> 07:49.516
Attention!

07:49.616 --> 07:53.519
Evacuate immediately!

07:53.559 --> 07:53.960
Attention!

07:54.000 --> 07:54.941
Evacuate immediately!

07:55.121 --> 07:55.541
Attention!

07:55.581 --> 07:56.682
Evacuate immediately!

08:06.290 --> 08:07.131
Go, go, go!

08:07.691 --> 08:08.172
It's coming!

08:08.192 --> 08:09.113
Get down!

